# Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 — GRAPH-MODE (lazy) SS lever. Clone of qwen36-27b.env, flipped eager -> lazy graph.
# =================================================================================================
# WHY (the lever): the base champion runs EAGER (PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0 + torch.compile). Under eager the
#   GDN forward is split across @torch._dynamo.disable graph-breaks (l2norm, recurrent general-path,
#   ssm-state save) + natural breaks (get_forward_context), so those ops fall back to op-by-op EAGER
#   dispatch = many small UNFUSED device kernels. On-card step-timer (SS bs=1): exec_med ~30.8ms /
#   gap_med ~0.3ms => DEVICE-exec-bound (~22x the ~1.4ms fp8-27B-TP8 BW ceiling), NOT host-bound.
#   LAZY mode is the graph mode: with per-DecoderLayer mark_step (modify_model_layers, interval=1)
#   each layer's WHOLE op sequence -- GDN scan + conv1d + fp8 GEMMs + norms -- JIT-fuses into ONE
#   Synapse recipe -> fewer/larger device kernels -> less exec time -> faster SS.
#
# WHY LAZY CRASHED BEFORE (and why this is safe now): under PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1 vLLM-gaudi skips
#   torch.compile and, during WARMUP, compiles a MULTIMODAL/VISION graph (warmup_model ->
#   warmup_multimodal_graphs -> embed_multimodal -> the Qwen3-VL vision tower). That vision warmup
#   graph compile is the synStatus-26 ("guid does not exist") site (the base-env note; "hybrid+fp8+
#   VISION"). PROOF it is NOT the GDN/fp8 ops: the Qwen3.5-A17B (397B) hybrid -- SAME GatedDeltaNet +
#   fp8 ops -- serves fine in lazy; the 27B-only difference is the VL vision tower. And the GDN decode
#   path is device-to-host-sync-FREE (the single-token fast path in ops/hpu_gdn_pytorch.py uses
#   shape-only detection, no .item()/.tolist()), so the language-model forward is capturable.
#   MITIGATIONS stacked here:
#     * VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true  -> skips warmup_multimodal_graphs (the vision crash) AND warmup_graphs.
#     * We serve TEXT ONLY (no image tokens) -> the vision tower is NEVER invoked at inference.
#     * --enforce-eager (in LAZY mode) -> makes _use_graphs() return False -> bypass_hpu_graphs=True:
#       the model's whole-forward wrap_in_hpu_graph replays NOTHING and runs the forward in plain
#       LAZY. So each layer is still fused per-mark_step (the device-time win) but the single opaque
#       WHOLE-FORWARD capture (the other potential crash / D2H-during-capture site) is skipped. On
#       HPU, --enforce-eager only toggles HPU-graph replay; it does NOT disable lazy fusion and does
#       NOT disable --async-scheduling (async is only turned off for spec-decode; platform.py:246).
#
# GATES (run in order): 1) serve comes up, no synStatus-26. 2) greedy COHERENCE (Paris / 144 / first
#   10 primes) -- watch the fp8<->bf16-GDN boundary for NaN/garbage (the 397B lesson). 3) step-timer:
#   exec_med must DROP from ~30.8ms (proof the layers fused). 4) SS c1 tok/s vs eager base 33.1 /
#   dynshapes 39.1. Then a c8 point for concurrency.
#
# UPGRADE (best fusion, slightly riskier -- fuses ACROSS layers into ONE replay per step): REMOVE
#   `--enforce-eager` from VLLM_ARGS. With VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP the whole-forward HPU graph then captures
#   on the FIRST text request. If it serves + coheres it should beat the per-layer path; if it
#   synStatus-26's, revert (put --enforce-eager back = this safe per-layer path).
#
# CODE-FLAG ALTERNATIVE (only if you bind-mount the patched _src plugin tree, as the glm52-async /
#   layerfuse serves do): a gated, model-scoped equivalent of the --enforce-eager bypass was added to
#   _src/vllm_gaudi/v1/worker/hpu_model_runner.py (_use_graphs: QWEN_HYBRID_NO_WHOLEGRAPH=1 -> return
#   False, default-off = byte-identical). To use it instead of --enforce-eager, DROP --enforce-eager
#   and add:  EXTRA_MOUNTS="-v $HOME/AI/_src/vllm_gaudi:/opt/vllm-gaudi/vllm_gaudi"  and
#   `-e QWEN_HYBRID_NO_WHOLEGRAPH=1` to MODEL_ENV. NOTE: that mounts the whole (~1100-line-divergent,
#   default-gated) dev tree over the in-image plugin, so for a CLEAN eager-vs-lazy A/B prefer the
#   no-mount --enforce-eager route above (identical bypass, in-image plugin).
#
# OPTIONAL extra SS lever (accuracy tradeoff -- gate coherence): add `-e VLLM_GDN_COMPUTE_FP32=0` to
#   run the GatedDeltaNet scan in bf16 instead of the fp32 default (~halves GDN decode compute).
#
# DEFAULT-SAFE: without this file the base qwen36-27b.env stays eager; nothing regresses. This env is
#   an opt-in A/B -- only PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE, --enforce-eager, and lazy collectives differ from base.
# =================================================================================================
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.6-27B-FP8
SERVED_NAME=qwen36-27b
# LAZY graph mode + skip warmup (vision-crash avoidance) + lazy TP8 collectives (graphs the all-reduce,
# the 397B-sslazy8 win). util 0.10: lazy recipe cache needs a little more room than eager's 0.04;
# lower it after it serves if co-residing under GLM.
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true -e PT_HPU_ENABLE_LAZY_COLLECTIVES=true -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=1800 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e VLLM_DECODE_BS_BUCKET_MIN=1 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.10 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true"
# --enforce-eager here = the SAFE per-layer lazy graph (bypass the whole-forward capture); see header.
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization fp8 --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --tensor-parallel-size 8 --max-model-len 2048 --max-num-seqs 16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.10 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code --enforce-eager"
